stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12.4 9.2v3.6a1.2 1.2 0 0 1-1.2 1.2h-8A1.2 1.2 0 0 1 2 12.8v-8a1.2 1.2 0 0 1 1.2-1.2h3.6"></path></svg><h4 class="font-mono text-[13px] leading-none font-medium -tracking-snug uppercase">TL;DR</h4></div><div class="admonition-text mt-2.5 text-base leading-normal tracking-extra-tight text-gray-new-20 dark:text-gray-new-85 [&amp;_a]:rounded-sm [&amp;_li]:text-base [&amp;_li]:leading-snug [&amp;_li]:tracking-extra-tight [&amp;_ul]:my-0 [&amp;_ol]:my-0"><p>If your app has variable traffic, here&#x27;s how Neon can save you time and money:</p><ul><li>Databases autoscale. CPU and memory scale up and down automatically. When you see traffic spikes, your database provisions more compute automatically; when traffic dies, it scales down.</li><li>You pay only for the compute you use. No downtime, no manual work.</li></ul><p>We have a Free Plan - <a href="https://console.neon.tech/signup">Get started here</a></p></div></div></div><figure class="not-prose relative mt-7 w-full rounded-lg bg-[#0D0E10] p-14 pr-11 pb-8 before:absolute before:top-6 before:left-6 before:size-16 before:bg-[url(&quot;/images/pages/variable-load/blockquote.svg&quot;)] before:bg-contain before:bg-no-repeat xl:mt-6 lg:mt-5 lg:p-12 lg:pr-10 lg:pb-7 sm:mt-4 sm:p-6 sm:pb-7 lg:before:top-[22px] lg:before:left-[22px] lg:before:size-14 sm:before:hidden"><div class="relative z-10"><blockquote class="text-lg leading-snug tracking-tighter">Our database traffic peaks at nights and on weekends. Building on a database that preemptively autoscales allows us to regularly handle these traffic spikes.</blockquote><div class="mt-5 flex items-center justify-between sm:mt-2.5 sm:flex-col sm:items-start sm:gap-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-2"><figcaption class="text-lg/normal text-gray-new-60 lg:text-base sm:text-sm/normal">Lex Nasser<cite class="font-light text-gray-new-40 not-italic"> <!-- -->- <!-- -->Founding Engineer at 222</cite></figcaption></div><a class="text-white transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-primary-2 group gap-1 sm:wrap-anywhere flex w-fit items-center text-sm leading-none font-medium tracking-[-0.03em]" href="/blog/how-222-uses-neon-to-handle-their-frequent-spikes-in-demand"><span>Case study</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="12" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 12" class="-mb-px size-3.5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-[3px]"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-width="1.4" d="M11.108 10.921 15 7.03l-3.892-3.892M.938 7.032h12.728"></path></svg></a></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 overflow-hidden rounded-[inherit]" aria-hidden="true"><div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] border border-white mix-blend-overlay"></div></div></figure></section><div class="load"><h2 class="group relative mb-7 w-fit pt-[72px] text-[36px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-tighter text-pretty xl:mb-6 xl:pt-16 xl:text-[32px] lg:mb-5 lg:pt-14 lg:text-[28px] md:mb-4 md:pt-11 md:text-2xl" id="fixed-compute-manual-resizes-extra-costs"><span>Fixed Compute = Manual Resizes, Extra Costs</span><a class="anchor inline-flex items-center justify-center px-2.5 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 sm:hidden" href="#fixed-compute-manual-resizes-extra-costs"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="size-5 text-green-45"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><div class="prose-variable"><p>Variable load patterns are common, but traditional managed databases require provisioning a fixed amount of CPU and memory.</p><p>To avoid performance issues during traffic spikes, you’re likely provisioning a larger machine than you need most of the time. Scaling up must be done manually. Scaling down may require downtime.</p></div><div class="mt-7 flex items-center justify-center gap-5 xl:mt-6 lg:mt-5 lg:flex-col md:gap-3.5 sm:mt-4"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="470" height="338" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[470px] shrink-0 rounded-lg lg:w-full lg:max-w-xl md:rounded" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 340px, 100vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 640w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 750w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 828w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-aws.0_r15m_p_mma3.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="470" height="338" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[470px] shrink-0 rounded-lg lg:w-full lg:max-w-xl md:rounded" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 340px, 100vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 640w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 750w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 828w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fload-graphic-neon.0kcxwzq27-d.v.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></div></div><div class="efficiency"><h2 class="group relative mb-7 w-fit pt-[72px] text-[36px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-tighter text-pretty xl:mb-6 xl:pt-16 xl:text-[32px] lg:mb-5 lg:pt-14 lg:text-[28px] md:mb-4 md:pt-11 md:text-2xl" id="neon-autoscaling-fixes-this-problem"><span>Neon Autoscaling Fixes This Problem</span><a class="anchor inline-flex items-center justify-center px-2.5 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 sm:hidden" href="#neon-autoscaling-fixes-this-problem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="size-5 text-green-45"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><div class="prose-variable"><ul class="max-w-[608px] space-y-4 pl-8 xl:space-y-3.5 lg:space-y-3 md:space-y-2.5 sm:pl-0"><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative mt-0.5 mr-3.5 flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded bg-variable-list-icon-bg sm:mt-0 sm:mr-3"><img class="relative" src="/_next/static/media/autoscale.03dpkxh9aot-b.svg?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7" alt="" loading="lazy" width="16" height="16"/><div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] border-image-variable-list-icon-border mix-blend-overlay"></div></div><div class="">Neon runs on serverless Postgres. Instead of provisioning a fixed CPU/memory, you specify an autoscaling range. </div></li><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative mt-0.5 mr-3.5 flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded bg-variable-list-icon-bg sm:mt-0 sm:mr-3"><img class="relative" src="/_next/static/media/performance.0w1pmobd_z46w.svg?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7" alt="" loading="lazy" width="16" height="16"/><div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] border-image-variable-list-icon-border mix-blend-overlay"></div></div><div class="">Your database will autoscale up and down automatically between those limits, matching your app’s traffic.</div></li><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative mt-0.5 mr-3.5 flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded bg-variable-list-icon-bg sm:mt-0 sm:mr-3"><img class="relative" src="/_next/static/media/resize.17fmtslv9_h10.svg?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7" alt="" loading="lazy" width="16" height="16"/><div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] border-image-variable-list-icon-border mix-blend-overlay"></div></div><div class="">Autoscaling is nearly instantaneous, without downtime. Read about <a href="/docs/guides/autoscaling-algorithm">our autoscaling algorithm</a> and how it compares to other serverless databases.</div></li></ul></div><figure class="not-prose relative mt-7 w-full rounded-lg bg-[#0D0E10] p-14 pr-11 pb-8 before:absolute before:top-6 before:left-6 before:size-16 before:bg-[url(&quot;/images/pages/variable-load/blockquote.svg&quot;)] before:bg-contain before:bg-no-repeat xl:mt-6 lg:mt-5 lg:p-12 lg:pr-10 lg:pb-7 sm:mt-4 sm:p-6 sm:pb-7 lg:before:top-[22px] lg:before:left-[22px] lg:before:size-14 sm:before:hidden"><div class="relative z-10"><blockquote class="text-lg leading-snug tracking-tighter">When we were using MySQL in Azure, we had to manually upgrade the database during the days of peak traffic and downgrade later in the day, which caused a couple of minutes of downtime and a huge waste of time for the team.</blockquote><div class="mt-5 flex items-center justify-between sm:mt-2.5 sm:flex-col sm:items-start sm:gap-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-2"><img alt="Pieralberto Colombo" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="size-8 rounded-full grayscale lg:size-7 sm:size-5" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fpieralberto-colonbo.0np6c8kwkkaxy.jpg&amp;w=32&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fpieralberto-colonbo.0np6c8kwkkaxy.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fpieralberto-colonbo.0np6c8kwkkaxy.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/><figcaption class="text-lg/normal text-gray-new-60 lg:text-base sm:text-sm/normal">Pieralberto Colombo<cite class="font-light text-gray-new-40 not-italic"> <!-- -->- <!-- -->Recrowd</cite></figcaption></div><a class="text-white transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-primary-2 group gap-1 sm:wrap-anywhere flex w-fit items-center text-sm leading-none font-medium tracking-[-0.03em]" href="/blog/how-recrowd-uses-neon-autoscaling-to-meet-fluctuating-demand"><span>Case study</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="12" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 12" class="-mb-px size-3.5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-[3px]"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-width="1.4" d="M11.108 10.921 15 7.03l-3.892-3.892M.938 7.032h12.728"></path></svg></a></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 overflow-hidden rounded-[inherit]" aria-hidden="true"><div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] border border-white mix-blend-overlay"></div></div></figure></div><div class="unique"><h2 class="group relative mb-7 w-fit pt-[72px] text-[36px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-tighter text-pretty xl:mb-6 xl:pt-16 xl:text-[32px] lg:mb-5 lg:pt-14 lg:text-[28px] md:mb-4 md:pt-11 md:text-2xl" id="neon-vs-other-serverless-databases"><span>Neon vs other serverless databases</span><a class="anchor inline-flex items-center justify-center px-2.5 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 sm:hidden" href="#neon-vs-other-serverless-databases"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="size-5 text-green-45"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><div class="prose-variable"><p>The Neon architecture is unique in the following ways:</p><ul class="max-w-[608px] space-y-4 pl-8 xl:space-y-3.5 lg:space-y-3 md:space-y-2.5 sm:pl-0"><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative pl-3.5 before:absolute before:top-[11px] before:left-0 before:block before:size-1 before:rounded-[1px] before:bg-white">Neon compute costs are up to 80% cheaper vs other serverless databases.</div></li><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative pl-3.5 before:absolute before:top-[11px] before:left-0 before:block before:size-1 before:rounded-[1px] before:bg-white">Neon provisions instances in < 1 s, compared to other serverless databases which can take up to&nbsp;20&nbsp;min.</div></li><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative pl-3.5 before:absolute before:top-[11px] before:left-0 before:block before:size-1 before:rounded-[1px] before:bg-white">Neon uses transparent compute units, vs abstractions used in other serverless databases.</div></li><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative pl-3.5 before:absolute before:top-[11px] before:left-0 before:block before:size-1 before:rounded-[1px] before:bg-white">Neon supports database branching with data and schema via copy-on-write, improving development workflows.</div></li><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative pl-3.5 before:absolute before:top-[11px] before:left-0 before:block before:size-1 before:rounded-[1px] before:bg-white">Neon&apos;s read replicas don&apos;t require storage redundancy, differently than other serverless databases.</div></li><li class="flex items-start"><div class="relative pl-3.5 before:absolute before:top-[11px] before:left-0 before:block before:size-1 before:rounded-[1px] before:bg-white">Connection pooling is built-in in Neon, unlike some other serverless databases that require separate proxies.</div></li></ul></div><figure class="not-prose relative mt-7 w-full rounded-lg bg-[#0D0E10] p-14 pr-11 pb-8 before:absolute before:top-6 before:left-6 before:size-16 before:bg-[url(&quot;/images/pages/variable-load/blockquote.svg&quot;)] before:bg-contain before:bg-no-repeat xl:mt-6 lg:mt-5 lg:p-12 lg:pr-10 lg:pb-7 sm:mt-4 sm:p-6 sm:pb-7 lg:before:top-[22px] lg:before:left-[22px] lg:before:size-14 sm:before:hidden"><div class="relative z-10"><blockquote class="text-lg leading-snug tracking-tighter">Neon worked out of the box, handling hundreds